{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:feasible-calibration",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Uniformly over \\(P\\in\\mathcal M\\),\n\\[\n |J|\\left(\\frac{c_gc_\\theta^2}{4V_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3}\n \\le\\mathcal V(P)\\le\n |J|\\left(\\frac{C_gC_\\theta^2}{4v_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3},\n\\]\nso \\(\\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal M}T_n(P)\\to\\infty\\). Separately, let \\(\\mathcal E(u)=\\beta u+\\gamma\\log u+c\\) with \\(\\beta>0\\), and restrict to an eventual domain on which \\(\\mathcal E'>0\\). Define \\(b_{\\mathcal E}(T)=\\mathcal E^{-1}(\\log T)\\) and \\(a_{\\mathcal E}(T)=1/\\mathcal E'(b_{\\mathcal E}(T))\\). If a future excursion theorem justifies this centering and scale and if \\(\\widehat{\\mathcal V}_n/\\mathcal V(P)=1+o_P(1)\\) uniformly, then\n\\[\n \\frac{b_{\\mathcal E}(\\widehat T_n)-b_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}{a_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}=o_P(1),\n \\qquad\n \\frac{a_{\\mathcal E}(\\widehat T_n)}{a_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}\\to1\n\\]\nuniformly. This conditional centering calculus does not establish an excursion law, a simulated-quantile approximation, or nominal coverage.",
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:spatial-clock",
      "thm:causal-transfer",
      "ass:strict-slope",
      "ass:variance"
    ],
    "justification": "Shows uniform positivity of the clock and the exact plug-in centering calculus conditional on a future affine-log excursion expansion.",
    "gap": "Clock consistency, the excursion law, transfer, random-horizon grid approximation, and anti-concentration remain missing.",
    "consumer": "No analytic or simulated nominal calibration follows.",
    "proof_tex": "The bounds \\(c_g\\le f(a)\\le C_g\\), proved in \\(\\texttt{thm:causal-transfer}\\), together with \\(\\texttt{ass:strict-slope}\\) and \\(\\texttt{ass:variance}\\), imply pointwise on \\(J\\)\n\\[\n \\left(\\frac{c_gc_\\theta^2}{4V_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3}\n \\le\n \\left\\{\\frac{f(a)\\theta'(a)^2}{4\\kappa(a)}\\right\\}^{1/3}\n \\le\n \\left(\\frac{C_gC_\\theta^2}{4v_\\kappa}\\right)^{1/3}.\n\\]\nIntegration over \\(J\\) proves the volume bounds. Since \\(\\delta\\in(0,1/2)\\), \\(|J|=1-2\\delta>0\\); thus the lower constant is positive. Multiplication by \\(n^{1/3}\\) proves \\(\\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal M}T_n(P)\\to\\infty\\).\n\nNow suppose the two explicit conditional premises in the second part hold. Relative clock consistency and \\(\\widehat T_n/T_n(P)=\\widehat{\\mathcal V}_n/\\mathcal V(P)\\) give\n\\[\n \\log\\frac{\\widehat T_n}{T_n(P)}=o_P(1)\n\\]\nuniformly. The deterministic lower bound just proved makes \\(T_n(P)\\to\\infty\\) uniformly; relative consistency then also makes \\(\\widehat T_n\\to\\infty\\) uniformly in probability. Hence both inverse centerings eventually lie in the increasing domain and diverge. By the mean-value theorem, for a point \\(\\widetilde b_n\\) between the two inverse centerings,\n\\[\n \\mathcal E'(\\widetilde b_n)\n \\{b_{\\mathcal E}(\\widehat T_n)-b_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P))\\}\n =\\log\\frac{\\widehat T_n}{T_n(P)}.\n\\]\nSince \\(\\mathcal E'(u)=\\beta+\\gamma/u\\to\\beta>0\\),\n\\[\n \\frac{b_{\\mathcal E}(\\widehat T_n)-b_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}{a_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}\n =\\frac{\\mathcal E'(b_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P)))}{\\mathcal E'(\\widetilde b_n)}\n \\log\\frac{\\widehat T_n}{T_n(P)}\n =o_P(1).\n\\]\nThe same derivative limit gives\n\\[\n \\frac{a_{\\mathcal E}(\\widehat T_n)}{a_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P))}\n =\\frac{\\mathcal E'(b_{\\mathcal E}(T_n(P)))}{\\mathcal E'(b_{\\mathcal E}(\\widehat T_n))}\n \\to1.\n\\]\nThese are implications of the stipulated future excursion form and clock consistency; neither premise is proved by this calculus.",
